  "decision_conditions": [
    "The change of use into a house of multiple occupation (HMO) results in more than one property out of a consecutive row of five properties being converted and results in a clustering of conversions along this terrace of buildings, unduly at odds with the predominant pattern of single family dwellinghouses along the road, contrary to Policies CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010) and DMD5 and DMD 37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014) and National Planning Policy Framework (2026).",
    "The proposed loft bedroom, by reason of its reliance on rooflights resulting in limited outlook and natural light, together with the inadequate functional floor area arising from restricted floor-to-ceiling heights, would provide a poor quality living environment for future occupiers. The accommodation would fail to provide a satisfactory standard of residential amenity or high-quality, fit-for-purpose living accommodation, contrary to Chapter 14 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2026), Policies D3 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policies CP4 and CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD5, DMD8 and DMD 37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), the Enfield HMO Standards (2021), and the Housing Design Standards London Plan Guidance (2023).",
    "The applicant has failed to demonstrate, through the submission of a robust parking stress survey and supporting evidence, that the additional parking demand arising from the proposed 5-bedroom, 6-person House in Multiple Occupation (HMO) can be accommodated within the surrounding highway network without resulting in unacceptable parking stress, displacement parking, or harm to highway safety and the efficient operation of the local road network. In the absence of sufficient evidence to demonstrate that the transport impacts of the development would be acceptable, the proposal is contrary to Chapter 15 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2026), Policies T2, T4 and T6 of the London Plan (2021), Core Policy CP24 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), and Policy DMD45 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
